# Task 169-001 Plan — W3.1 C0c Collision Detection Live Trigger Fix

## RC Summary
`detectScopeCollisions` (conflict-resolver.ts) uses `file.trim()` only. Path variants
(`./src/foo.ts` vs `src/foo.ts`, `src//foo.ts`, `src/foo.ts/`) bypass the collision
threshold (each variant has 1 writer). The wire layer emits SPAWN:BLOCKED only when
paths match string-exact. Sprint 169 events.jsonl seq 1-4 shows this happens by
accident when both tasks use both variants — single-variant tasks slip through.

## Approach
1. Write RC doc → `.audit/sprint-169/W3.1-root-cause.md` (done).
2. Write failing TDD tests → `tests/orchestra/c0c-collision-live-fire.test.ts` (3 cases).
3. Add `normalizeScopeFiles` helper to `src/orchestra/sprint-spawner.ts`.
4. In `spawnWorkers`, pre-pass: clone pendingTasks with normalized `filesWrite` before
   calling `detectScopeCollisions(...)`.
5. Run tsc + vitest, fix any failures.

## Files To Modify
- src/orchestra/sprint-spawner.ts (add helper + integrate into spawnWorkers)
- tests/orchestra/c0c-collision-live-fire.test.ts (new, 3 tests)
- .audit/sprint-169/W3.1-root-cause.md (already written)

## Risk
- `conflict-resolver.ts` is out-of-scope (touching it would breach Auditor). Solution:
  pre-pass at call site keeps that file untouched.
- Wire change does not affect `respawnEligibleTasks` or `applyCascadeToSprint` (they
  use `buildDependencyGraph`, not `detectScopeCollisions`). No collateral risk.
- Existing `spawn-spawner-wire.test.ts` uses identical paths → normalize is no-op → no
  regression expected.

## Decision-Engine Touch
None. Plan §2.1 lists decision-engine as alternate fix location but RC is in pre-pass
normalization, not in the pure `handleScopeCollision` decision. Decision-engine stays
unchanged.
